      "cancellation_policy": {"supported": true},
      "reconciliation_policy": {"supported": true},
      "guidance": "Use this Operation for real SAM3 segmentation. Bind the authorized image Artifact as source. Start with one broad model-native category noun such as person, car, animal, or logo only when the source has one unambiguous target. When the source contains multiple candidates or the user requests separate subjects, use an inspected explicit box or points for each Job instead of repeating the same broad prompt. Compound marks and a text wordmark are unreliable prompt-only targets: use inspected box or points when semantic matting is required, or delegate a scoped Child Harness with the media-processing Skill for geometric crop or uniform-background removal. If no_target_found is returned, replace the Job with a broader category, box, or points; never repeat the same selector or substitute an approximate local segmentation algorithm. Dimension, alpha, and nontrivial-mask validators prove only structural validity, not that the requested subject was isolated; inspect each foreground semantically before publication and replace a wrong-target result with refined box or points. foreground is a transparent PNG, mask is a nontrivial grayscale PNG, and segmentation_report is JSON."
    },
